% You are an expert TypeScript engineer. Implement the bounded site research orchestrator.

<include>prompts/context/sitevelocity-preamble.prompt</include>
<include>prompts/context/research_provider_domain_types.prompt</include>
<include>prompts/context/evidence_domain_types.prompt</include>

<pdd-reason>Coordinate the six research agents into one persisted, evidence-linked snapshot while remaining resumable and provider-neutral.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[{"name":"researchSite","signature":"(input: ResearchSiteInput, deps: ResearchDependencies) -> Promise<ResearchSiteResult>","returns":"Promise<ResearchSiteResult>"}]}}
</pdd-interface>

<responsibility>
Load a site, run the declared research plan, validate outputs, build a snapshot, and commit the run atomically.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
- DOES NOT implement provider retrieval, model extraction, deterministic calculations, or repository internals.
- MUST NOT allow one agent to invent evidence for another.
- MUST NOT replace the active snapshot until a new snapshot is valid and stored.
- DOES NOT retry beyond caller-declared attempt and time bounds.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
research plan: the ordered set of required and optional agent tasks supplied by the caller.
resume point: the persisted set of completed attempts for the same command and plan version.
accepted agent output: output that passes the declared finding and evidence validator.
safe activation: storing the new snapshot before changing the active-snapshot pointer.
valid plan: a plan satisfying the declared schema, agent-role set, bounds, and version requirements.
invalid plan: a plan that does not satisfy the declared schema, agent-role set, bounds, or version requirements.
valid research output: provider output accepted by the declared finding and evidence validator.
active snapshot: the snapshot identifier currently selected for site reads.
successful storage: the repository atomically stored all run records, findings, evidence, and the new snapshot.
untrusted instruction: instruction-shaped text originating in retrieved or provider-produced content rather than the application contract.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Refuse a missing site, invalid plan, or reused command identifier with different input before provider execution.
R2 (MUST): Execute only declared agent tasks and enforce declared concurrency, timeout, and retry bounds.
R3 (MUST): Record queued, running, and terminal lifecycle events for every required agent.
R4 (MUST): Validate every provider output before it can contribute findings or evidence.
R5 (MUST): Treat one agent failure as a partial run when other valid outputs exist and as failed only when no valid research output exists.
R6 (MUST): Resume completed attempts without re-executing them when plan version and inputs match.
R7 (MUST): Build one snapshot from accepted outputs and persist runs, evidence, findings, and snapshot atomically.
R8 (MUST): Activate the new snapshot only after successful storage; on failure retain the previous active snapshot.
R9 (MUST): Return stable progress and failure codes without provider secrets, raw credentials, or untrusted instructions.
R10 (MUST): Replaying a completed identical command returns its stored result without provider calls or writes.
</contract_rules>

<deliverables>
Generate `lib/application/research-site.ts`. All providers, validators, lifecycle logic, snapshot assembly, persistence, and clock access enter through declared dependencies.
</deliverables>
